------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT YOU MAY DO
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. View, clone, and study this code for personal learning.
2. Take inspiration from the ideas, structure, patterns, and techniques here
   when building your own original work.
3. Adapt small, isolated techniques or patterns into a project that is
   substantially your own (different design, content, structure, and purpose).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Copy this project as a whole, or a substantial part of it, and present the
   result as your own original work or portfolio.
2. Redistribute this repository (or a lightly modified fork) as a template,
   starter kit, or "my portfolio" product under your name or brand.
3. Remove, alter, or obscure copyright, authorship, or license notices.
4. Use personal assets from this project as if they were yours. That includes,
   without limitation: photographs, portraits, signatures, logos, brand marks,
   copy written in Ted Brine's voice, and similar identity materials.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUBSTANTIAL COPYING
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Substantial" means more than incidental reuse. Examples that are not allowed
without prior written permission:

- Reusing most of the layout, visual design, and section structure with only
  names, colours, or images swapped
- Republishing large portions of the source with minor renames or restyling
- Shipping a near-duplicate site that a reasonable person would recognise as
  this portfolio with a different name on it

Taking a pattern you learned here and reimplementing it in a clearly original
project is fine. Shipping this site with your face and links is not.

